<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nubia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Nubian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nubia is the region along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, covering southern Egypt and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>. It was rich in gold and controlled trade routes to tropical <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. The Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a> conquered it and governed it through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-kush">Viceroy of Kush</a>, while Nubia was also the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushite-empire">Kushite Empire</a>, which later ruled Egypt.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nubia.jpg" alt="Nubia" width="320" height="261" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Matthias Gehricke · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rulers_of_Kush,_Kerma_Museum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
